From: Xios project <xios@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: build Crispy as a Unix SDL client on the Darwin/iOS target

The Procursus cross toolchain identifies the target as Darwin/iOS so CMake
emits Mach-O, but Xios runs Crispy Doom as an ordinary Wayland client through
the vendored xios-sdl2 (Unix Wayland backend, no UIKit). Crispy's sources
already take the generic Unix paths there (__MACOSX__ is not defined on iOS),
so the only target-specific piece is SDL's entry point: SDL_main.h on iOS
renames main() and expects SDL2main to supply a UIKit trampoline. Add an
explicit CRISPY_XIOS option that keeps Crispy's own main() (SDL_MAIN_HANDLED),
stops linking SDL2main, and exposes CRISPY_XIOS=1 to the sources.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -36,6 +36,14 @@
 option(ENABLE_SDL2_NET "Enable SDL2_net" On)
 option(ENABLE_SDL2_MIXER "Enable SDL2_mixer" On)
 
+# Xios: the Procursus toolchain targets iOS, where SDL_main.h expects SDL's
+# UIKit main trampoline. Xios runs Crispy as a plain Unix Wayland client, so
+# keep Crispy's own main() and let it mark SDL ready itself (i_main.c).
+option(CRISPY_XIOS "Build as an Xios Wayland client on the Darwin/iOS target" OFF)
+if(CRISPY_XIOS)
+    add_compile_definitions(CRISPY_XIOS=1 SDL_MAIN_HANDLED)
+endif()
+
 if (NOT DEFINED EMSCRIPTEN)
     find_package(SDL2 2.0.14)
 endif()
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -45,7 +45,11 @@
         set(CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS "${CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS} -s USE_SDL_NET=2")
     endif()
 else()
-    set(SDL_LINK_LIBS SDL2::SDL2main SDL2::SDL2)
+    if(CRISPY_XIOS)
+        set(SDL_LINK_LIBS SDL2::SDL2)
+    else()
+        set(SDL_LINK_LIBS SDL2::SDL2main SDL2::SDL2)
+    endif()
     if(ENABLE_SDL2_MIXER)
         list(APPEND SDL_LINK_LIBS SDL2_mixer::SDL2_mixer)
     endif()
